course: dictionary
lesson: 3448
title: Facility: a place, a service or a talent
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A facility is a building, room or piece of equipment made for a special purpose, like a sports facility. Facilities are the things provided for people to use. When you meet facility, read the words around it to find out which meaning fits.
explain: «Where are the facilities?» The word where tells you someone is looking for a place. Here facilities is a polite word for the toilet. Polite words like this are called euphemisms, because they say something gently.
explain: Formal and official texts use facility as a stiff word for a place or building. «Correctional facility» is the US official word for a prison. In a sentence like «Mia has a real facility for languages», the clue is that she is good at something, so facility means an easy ability.
fact: A facility is a building, room or piece of equipment made for a special purpose.
fact: Facilities are things provided for people to use, like toilets, showers and car parks.
fact: A facility for something means an easy ability to do it, such as a facility for languages.
fact: «The facilities» can be a polite way to say the toilet.
fact: «Correctional facility» is the US official word for a prison.
exercise: «Where are the facilities?» What does facilities most likely mean here? | A library book | A football pitch | The school bus | *The toilets
exercise: Which of these is a sports facility? | A sunny afternoon | *A swimming pool built for people to swim in | A kind of dog | A slice of cake
exercise: Mia has a real facility for languages. What does facility mean here? | *An easy natural ability | A large building | A toilet | A rule that says no
test: A sign says «Toilet facilities available». What does it tell you? | Toilets are for sale | *Toilets can be used here | The school has no toilets | The toilets are broken
test: In US official writing, what does «correctional facility» mean? | A shop | A park | *A prison | A library
exam: Which phrase is a polite word for the toilet? | Sports facilities | Leisure facilities | Research facility | *The facilities
